00:45:10,510 --> 00:45:14,270
come back and have more time for questions soon.

1042
00:45:14,270 --> 00:45:19,105
So here is a fully connected layer with learnable parameters

1043
00:45:19,105 --> 00:45:21,230
for how to take a weighted combination of the input

1044
00:45:21,230 --> 00:45:23,910
token sequence to the output token sequence.

1045
00:45:23,910 --> 00:45:26,530
And here is the idea of self-attention,

1046
00:45:26,530 --> 00:45:29,590
which is that the weights of that linear combination

1047
00:45:29,590 --> 00:45:31,840
are a function of the input sequence.

1048
00:45:31,840 --> 00:45:37,600
So the F that's going to determine our queries and keys,

1049
00:45:37,600 --> 00:45:39,840
or in particular our queries, is going

1050
00:45:39,840 --> 00:45:45,600
to be coming from the input token sequence T in.

1051
00:45:45,600 --> 00:45:47,680
So how is it going to come from them?

1052
00:45:47,680 --> 00:45:52,160
It's going to be exactly the same type of math

1053
00:45:52,160 --> 00:45:54,140
that I showed you a few slides back.

1054
00:45:54,140 --> 00:45:56,600
But here's how it looks for self-attention.

1055
00:45:56,600 --> 00:45:58,300
So I have my T in.

1056
00:45:58,300 --> 00:46:00,520
And every single token in my input sequence

1057
00:46:00,520 --> 00:46:04,200
is going to emit a key, a value, and a query vector.

1058
00:46:04,200 --> 00:46:08,600
It's going to emit those via WQ, which

1059
00:46:08,600 --> 00:46:12,240
is a projection from its token vector into a query vector

1060
00:46:12,240 --> 00:46:15,240
WK, which is a projection from its token vectors

1061
00:46:15,240 --> 00:46:18,120
to its key vector, and the same for the value vector.

1062
00:46:18,120 --> 00:46:23,120
So now I will get a set of queries, a set of keys,

1063
00:46:23,120 --> 00:46:24,260
and a set of values.

1064
00:46:24,260 --> 00:46:28,040
I can stack them up into the query matrix, which

1065
00:46:28,040 --> 00:46:29,840
is for every row in that matrix it will

1066
00:46:29,840 --> 00:46:32,160
be the query for one of my input tokens,

1067
00:46:32,160 --> 00:46:35,200
for every key matrix and the value matrix.

1068
00:46:35,200 --> 00:46:41,280
And this is just saying that I can represent the query matrix

1069
00:46:41,280 --> 00:46:44,900
as just the matrix product of-- it's just a matmul,

1070
00:46:44,900 --> 00:46:49,760
it's just a matrix multiply of the token matrix

1071
00:46:49,760 --> 00:46:56,360
times the learnable projection to queries.

1072
00:46:56,360 --> 00:47:00,040
So this is another nice thing about the design of transformers

1073
00:47:00,040 --> 00:47:03,800
is everything just becomes these matrix multiplies in a very

1074
00:47:03,800 --> 00:47:05,380
simple, notational form.

1075
00:47:05,380 --> 00:47:07,040
So this is my queries.

1076
00:47:07,040 --> 00:47:10,920
And they're just T in times WQ.

1077
00:47:10,920 --> 00:47:15,040
So now I take all of these matrices.

1078
00:47:15,040 --> 00:47:18,880
And in order to get the weight in the linear combination

1079
00:47:18,880 --> 00:47:22,710
for this unit of T out from this unit of T in-- so remember,

1080
00:47:22,710 --> 00:47:24,460
the linear combination is over the values.

1081
00:47:24,460 --> 00:47:26,220
The values are in this teal color.

1082
00:47:26,220 --> 00:47:28,770
So I'm going to take a linear combination over the values.

1083
00:47:28,770 --> 00:47:31,465
And the weight that I'll assign to that linear combination is

1084
00:47:31,465 --> 00:47:34,090
going to be the inner product, the dot product, between the key

1085
00:47:34,090 --> 00:47:38,910
and the query for this token

1086
00:47:38,910 --> 00:47:42,770
So the amount of self-attention that I apply to myself

1087
00:47:42,770 --> 00:47:44,930
is going to be given by this gray box, which

1088
00:47:44,930 --> 00:47:46,850
is just this dot product.

1089
00:47:46,850 --> 00:47:49,870
And if you work out the linear algebra,

1090
00:47:49,870 --> 00:47:51,690
you can realize that this will just

1091
00:47:51,690 --> 00:47:57,570
be the matrix multiply of the query times the key matrix.

1092
00:47:57,570 --> 00:47:59,650
And then that will just be every query vector

1093
00:47:59,650 --> 00:48:03,870
gets multiplied by every key vector.

1094
00:48:03,870 --> 00:48:05,370
And that results in the value.

1095
00:48:05,370 --> 00:48:09,810
And the values will then be stacked up into an n

1096
00:48:09,810 --> 00:48:10,490
by n matrix.

1097
00:48:10,490 --> 00:48:12,990
I'll have n input tokens to n output tokens.

1098
00:48:12,990 --> 00:48:15,730
That's an n by n set of weights that determine

1099
00:48:15,730 --> 00:48:16,950
that linear combination.

1100
00:48:19,650 --> 00:48:23,010
So mathematically, we can condense all of this

1101
00:48:23,010 --> 00:48:24,270
into this simple equation.

1102
00:48:24,270 --> 00:48:26,410
This is the famous attention equation,

1103
00:48:26,410 --> 00:48:30,370
which is going to be the query matrix times the key matrix

1104
00:48:30,370 --> 00:48:31,490
transpose.

1105
00:48:31,490 --> 00:48:34,250
So if I transpose, I'm going to be

1106
00:48:34,250 --> 00:48:36,770
taking the dot product between all the pairs of queries

1107
00:48:36,770 --> 00:48:38,170
and keys.

1108
00:48:38,170 --> 00:48:42,490
And then I'll divide by the square root

1109
00:48:42,490 --> 00:48:48,850
of the dimensionality of the vectors.

1110
00:48:48,850 --> 00:48:51,270
So the keys' queries and values are M dimensional vectors.

1111
00:48:51,270 --> 00:48:52,110
They don't have to be the same.

1112
00:48:52,110 --> 00:48:53,110
They don't have to be D dimensional.

1113
00:48:53,110 --> 00:48:54,470
Remember, the tokens were D dimensional,

1114
00:48:54,470 --> 00:48:56,262
but in general the queries' keys and values

1115
00:48:56,262 --> 00:48:57,890
could be of some other dimensionality.

1116
00:48:57,890 --> 00:48:59,770
I'll divide by that dimensionality.

1117
00:48:59,770 --> 00:49:03,050
And then I'll take a softmax to ensure that everything

1118
00:49:03,050 --> 00:49:04,190
sums to 1.

1119
00:49:04,190 --> 00:49:05,810
So that has some nice normalization

1120
00:49:05,810 --> 00:49:07,770
and numerical advantages.

1121
00:49:07,770 --> 00:49:09,370
And then finally, the output will just

1122
00:49:09,370 --> 00:49:17,010
be the attention matrix times the value matrix of the input

1123
00:49:17,010 --> 00:49:18,610
set of tokens.

1124
00:49:18,610 --> 00:49:22,090
So it's a lot of little nitty-gritty linear algebra

1125
00:49:22,090 --> 00:49:23,340
to work out.

1126
00:49:23,340 --> 00:49:28,220
But it comes to a very simple equation in the end.

1127
00:49:28,220 --> 00:49:29,450
Yeah.

1128
00:49:29,450 --> 00:49:32,220
AUDIENCE: Like, is there a good intuitive reason

1129
00:49:32,220 --> 00:49:35,980
for why we bother learning parameters or matrices

1130
00:49:35,980 --> 00:49:39,660
for human case separately, rather than learning the values

1131
00:49:39,660 --> 00:49:41,220
of the A matrix directly?

1132
00:49:41,220 --> 00:49:43,220
At the end of the day, T in is going

1133
00:49:43,220 --> 00:49:46,340
to be a matrix multiply, which is

1134
00:49:46,340 --> 00:49:49,100
a function of two learned matrices, which

1135
00:49:49,100 --> 00:49:52,355
is A. Dot product with another learned matrix, which

1136
00:49:52,355 --> 00:49:52,980
is [INAUDIBLE].

1137
00:49:52,980 --> 00:49:53,855
PHILLIP ISOLA: Right.

1138
00:49:53,855 --> 00:49:56,100
AUDIENCE: So is there something about decomposing A

1139
00:49:56,100 --> 00:50:02,280
into the product of Q and K that leads to like--

1140
00:50:02,280 --> 00:50:04,220
I'm not asking for a theoretical argument.

1141
00:50:04,220 --> 00:50:06,840
PHILLIP ISOLA: Yeah, no, no, it's a good question.

1142
00:50:06,840 --> 00:50:08,680
Like, why not learn A directly?

1143
00:50:11,780 --> 00:50:13,300
The basic statement is empirically

1144
00:50:13,300 --> 00:50:14,420
the transformer recipe--

1145
00:50:14,420 --> 00:50:17,180
I'll specify it-- just seems to work the best at so

1146
00:50:17,180 --> 00:50:19,700
many different things.

1147
00:50:19,700 --> 00:50:22,140
I don't know about direct comparisons between learning

1148
00:50:22,140 --> 00:50:25,020
A versus using this outer product

1149
00:50:25,020 --> 00:50:28,560
of the queries and the keys that are also learnable projections.

1150
00:50:28,560 --> 00:50:31,980
But you can start to count how many learnable parameters there

1151
00:50:31,980 --> 00:50:33,060
are and what is.

1152
00:50:33,060 --> 00:50:36,300
So at the end of the day, we have some parameterized mapping

1153
00:50:36,300 --> 00:50:37,320
from T in to T out.

1154
00:50:37,320 --> 00:50:40,380
And you can think, if I learned A directly, I

1155
00:50:40,380 --> 00:50:43,100
would have to learn n squared parameters,

1156
00:50:43,100 --> 00:50:46,220
where n is the number of tokens in my sequence.

1157
00:50:46,220 --> 00:50:50,910
If I learn WQ, WK, and WV, I'm also

1158
00:50:50,910 --> 00:50:52,660
learning a lot of parameters, but it's not

1159
00:50:52,660 --> 00:50:54,035
dependent on the sequence length.

1160
00:50:54,035 --> 00:50:55,900
Now it's dependent on the dimensionality

1161
00:50:55,900 --> 00:50:57,640
of my token vectors.

1162
00:50:57,640 --> 00:50:59,980
So it's dependent on D, as opposed to n.

1163
00:50:59,980 --> 00:51:03,260
Now transformers are typically applied in modern AI

1164
00:51:03,260 --> 00:51:05,760
to extremely long sequences of tokens,

1165
00:51:05,760 --> 00:51:09,780
maybe like length million sequences of tokens, even.

1166
00:51:09,780 --> 00:51:13,780
Like, modern LLMs, you can have paragraphs and paragraphs

1167
00:51:13,780 --> 00:51:16,060
and whole books that you're processing.

1168
00:51:16,060 --> 00:51:18,572
So n is usually very large, and D is much smaller.

1169
00:51:18,572 --> 00:51:20,530
So there's actually fewer learnable parameters.

1170
00:51:20,530 --> 00:51:23,270
That's just one perspective.

1171
00:51:23,270 --> 00:51:24,170
OK, one more.

1172
00:51:24,170 --> 00:51:27,310
AUDIENCE: Yeah, I just wonder if the size

1173
00:51:27,310 --> 00:51:31,230
of the I or n or a different tree

1174
00:51:31,230 --> 00:51:34,550
or different update for your neural network could be variable

1175
00:51:34,550 --> 00:51:36,590
or has to be fixed?

1176
00:51:36,590 --> 00:51:41,030
Because I feel like language is so different from images.

1177
00:51:41,030 --> 00:51:44,870
